<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For every <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in M</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote by <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{\kappa}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{\kappa}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> the largest eigenvalue of the curvature operator of <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(x)\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(x)\in B</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{\lambda}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{\lambda}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> the lowest eigenvalue of the Ricci curvature of
<math id="S2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(x)\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(x)\in B</annotation></semantics></math> (thus <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> are constant along each fibre), and <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> the largest eigenvalue of the Ricci curvature of the fibre at <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then we are ready to state the Simons-type integral inequalities derived by the DDVV-type inequality for real skew-symmetric matrices.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2.7</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Ge<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>)<span id="S2.Thmthm7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:M^{n+m}\rightarrow B^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:M^{n+m}\rightarrow B^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Riemannian submersion with totally geodesic fibres and
Yang-Mills horizontal distribution, and suppose <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is compact.</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

