<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3. </span>New progress on DDVV-type inequalities</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To describe the equality condition in this section, we put <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{K}(n,m):=U(n)\times O(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{K}(n,m):=U(n)\times O(m)</annotation></semantics></math>.
A <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{K}(n,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{K}(n,m)</annotation></semantics></math> action on a family of matrices <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{1},\cdots,A_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{1},\cdots,A_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P,R)\cdot(B_{1},\cdots,B_{m}):=(P^{*}B_{1}P,\cdots,P^{*}B_{m}P)\cdot R." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P,R)\cdot(B_{1},\cdots,B_{m}):=(P^{*}B_{1}P,\cdots,P^{*}B_{m}P)\cdot R.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1. </span>DDVV-type inequality for complex matrices</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to generalize the DDVV-type inequality to complex matrices,
Ge-Xu-You-Zhou <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> first considered the complex matrices with symmetries, namely, the Hermitian matrices and the skew-Hermitian matrices.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Ge-Xu-You-Zhou <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>)<span id="S3.Thmthm1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1},\cdots,B_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1},\cdots,B_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times n</annotation></semantics></math> (skew-)Hermitian matrices, <math id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{m}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\leq\frac{4}{3}\left(\sum^{m}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{m}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\leq\frac{4}{3}\left(\sum^{m}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the equality holds if and only if there exists a </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P,R)\in\widetilde{K}(n,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P,R)\in\widetilde{K}(n,m)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P,R)\cdot(B_{1},\cdots,B_{m})=(\diag(H_{1},0),\diag(H_{2},0),\diag(H_{3},0),0,\cdots,0)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P,R)\cdot(B_{1},\cdots,B_{m})=(\diag(H_{1},0),\diag(H_{2},0),\diag(H_{3},0),0,\cdots,0),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where for some </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}:=\begin{pmatrix}\lambda&amp;0\\
0&amp;-\lambda\\
\end{pmatrix},H_{2}:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;\lambda\\
\lambda&amp;0\\
\end{pmatrix},H_{3}:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-\lambda\mathbf{i}\\
\lambda\mathbf{i}&amp;0\\
\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>λ</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>λ</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>λ</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐢</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐢</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}:=\begin{pmatrix}\lambda&amp;0\\
0&amp;-\lambda\\
\end{pmatrix},H_{2}:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;\lambda\\
\lambda&amp;0\\
\end{pmatrix},H_{3}:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-\lambda\mathbf{i}\\
\lambda\mathbf{i}&amp;0\\
\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{2}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\leq\left(\sum^{2}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{2}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\leq\left(\sum^{2}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the equality holds if and only if
under some </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{K}(n,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{K}(n,2)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> action,
</span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}=diag(H_{1},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}=diag(H_{1},0)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}=diag(\cos\theta H_{2}+\sin\theta H_{3},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}=diag(\cos\theta H_{2}+\sin\theta H_{3},0)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Using the technique by dividing complex matrices into Hermitian matrices and skew-Hermitian matrices, Ge-Li-Zhou <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite> obtained the DDVV-type inequality for general complex matrices.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Ge-Li-Zhou <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>)<span id="S3.Thmthm2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1},\cdots,B_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1},\cdots,B_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be arbitrary <math id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times n</annotation></semantics></math> complex matrices, <math id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{m}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\leq\frac{4}{3}\left(\sum^{m}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{m}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\leq\frac{4}{3}\left(\sum^{m}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq r\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq r\leq m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, let </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{r}^{1}=\frac{1}{2}(B_{r}+B_{r}^{*}),B_{r}^{2}=\frac{1}{2}(B_{r}-B_{r}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{r}^{1}=\frac{1}{2}(B_{r}+B_{r}^{*}),B_{r}^{2}=\frac{1}{2}(B_{r}-B_{r}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.
The equality holds if and only if </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{m}_{r=1}\left[B_{r},B_{r}^{*}\right]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{m}_{r=1}\left[B_{r},B_{r}^{*}\right]=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and
there exists a </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P,R)\in\widetilde{K}(n,2m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P,R)\in\widetilde{K}(n,2m)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P,R)\cdot(B_{1}^{1},\cdots,B_{m}^{1},\mathbf{i}B_{1}^{2},\cdots,\mathbf{i}B_{m}^{2})=(\diag(H_{1},0),\diag(H_{2},0),\diag(H_{3},0),0,\cdots,0)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P,R)\cdot(B_{1}^{1},\cdots,B_{m}^{1},\mathbf{i}B_{1}^{2},\cdots,\mathbf{i}B_{m}^{2})=(\diag(H_{1},0),\diag(H_{2},0),\diag(H_{3},0),0,\cdots,0),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where for some </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}:=\begin{pmatrix}\lambda&amp;0\\
0&amp;-\lambda\\
\end{pmatrix},\quad H_{2}:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;\lambda\\
\lambda&amp;0\\
\end{pmatrix},\quad H_{3}:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-\lambda\mathbf{i}\\
\lambda\mathbf{i}&amp;0\\
\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>λ</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>λ</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>λ</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐢</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐢</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}:=\begin{pmatrix}\lambda&amp;0\\
0&amp;-\lambda\\
\end{pmatrix},\quad H_{2}:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;\lambda\\
\lambda&amp;0\\
\end{pmatrix},\quad H_{3}:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-\lambda\mathbf{i}\\
\lambda\mathbf{i}&amp;0\\
\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{2}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\leq\left(\sum^{2}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{2}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\leq\left(\sum^{2}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The equality holds if and only if there exists a unitary matrix </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
such that </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}=U^{*}\diag(\widetilde{B_{1}},0)U,B_{2}=U^{*}\diag(\widetilde{B_{2}},0)U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}=U^{*}\diag(\widetilde{B_{1}},0)U,B_{2}=U^{*}\diag(\widetilde{B_{2}},0)U</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,
where </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{B_{1}},\widetilde{B_{2}}\in M(2,\mathbb{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{B_{1}},\widetilde{B_{2}}\in M(2,\mathbb{C})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
with </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widetilde{B_{1}}\|=\|\widetilde{B_{2}}\|,\langle\widetilde{B_{1}},\widetilde{B_{2}}\rangle=0,\operatorname{tr}\widetilde{B_{1}}=\operatorname{tr}\widetilde{B_{2}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widetilde{B_{1}}\|=\|\widetilde{B_{2}}\|,\langle\widetilde{B_{1}},\widetilde{B_{2}}\rangle=0,\operatorname{tr}\widetilde{B_{1}}=\operatorname{tr}\widetilde{B_{2}}=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}:=\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\
0&amp;-1\\
\end{pmatrix},\quad B_{2}:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;1\\
1&amp;0\\
\end{pmatrix},\quad B_{3}:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-1\\
1&amp;0\\
\end{pmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}:=\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\
0&amp;-1\\
\end{pmatrix},\quad B_{2}:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;1\\
1&amp;0\\
\end{pmatrix},\quad B_{3}:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-1\\
1&amp;0\\
\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{3}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\ =\frac{4}{3}\left(\sum^{3}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2},\quad\sum^{2}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\ =\left(\sum^{2}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{3}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\ =\frac{4}{3}\left(\sum^{3}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2},\quad\sum^{2}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\ =\left(\sum^{2}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Hence the optimal constants for the real matrices case and the complex matrices case are both
<math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{4}{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{4}{3}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By slightly changing the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 3.2 (Ge-Li-Zhou []). ‣ 3.1. DDVV-type inequality for complex matrices ‣ 3. New progress on DDVV-type inequalities ‣ A survey on the DDVV-type inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>,
Ge-Li-Zhou <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite> also obtained the DDVV-type inequality for complex symmetric or complex skew-symmetric matrices.
See Table <a href="#S1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 1. Introduction of DDVV-type inequality ‣ A survey on the DDVV-type inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for the optimal constants.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2. </span>DDVV-type inequality for quaternionic matrices</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Ge-Li-Zhou <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite> generalized the BW inequality and the DDVV inequality to quaternionic matrices. In this case, it turns out that both of
the optimal constants <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> are double of that for complex matrices,
mainly because the multiplication of <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{i},\mathbf{j},\mathbf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐣</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐤</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{i},\mathbf{j},\mathbf{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is anti-commutative.
The proof is carried out simply by mapping a quaternionic matrix into a complex matrix and then using the known inequalities for complex matrices
in a fashion analogous to what they have done with proving Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Ge-Xu-You-Zhou []). ‣ 3.1. DDVV-type inequality for complex matrices ‣ 3. New progress on DDVV-type inequalities ‣ A survey on the DDVV-type inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(BW-type inequality for quaternionic matrices <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>)<span id="S3.Thmthm4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y\in M(n,\mathbb{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℍ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y\in M(n,\mathbb{H})</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|[X,Y]\|^{2}\leq 4\|X\|^{2}\|Y\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|[X,Y]\|^{2}\leq 4\|X\|^{2}\|Y\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The equality holds if and only if
either <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|X\|\|Y\|=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|X\|\|Y\|=0</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=upu^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=upu^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=uqu^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=uqu^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for some unit column vector <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{H}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℍ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{H}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in\mathbb{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℍ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in\mathbb{H}</annotation></semantics></math> are purely imaginary quaternions that have real-orthogonal vector representations in the canonical basis.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3.5</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The maximal pair <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math> can be rewritten as <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=U\diag(p,0,\cdots,0)U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=U\diag(p,0,\cdots,0)U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=U\diag(q,0,\cdots,0)U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=U\diag(q,0,\cdots,0)U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for some quaternionic unitary matrix <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in Sp(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in Sp(n)</annotation></semantics></math>. The condition on <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to the anti-commutativity <math id="S3.Thmthm5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pq=-qp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pq=-qp</annotation></semantics></math>, which cannot happen in the real or complex cases.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3.6</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\mathbf{i},~Y=\mathbf{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐢</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐣</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\mathbf{i},~Y=\mathbf{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\left[X,Y\right]\|^{2}=4\|X\|^{2}\|Y\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\left[X,Y\right]\|^{2}=4\|X\|^{2}\|Y\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Hence <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal constant for the BW-type inequality for quaternionic matrices.
Moreover, for any <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=xx^{t}\mathbf{i},~Y=\lambda xx^{t}\mathbf{j}\in M(n,\mathbb{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐢</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐣</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℍ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=xx^{t}\mathbf{i},~Y=\lambda xx^{t}\mathbf{j}\in M(n,\mathbb{H})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\left[X,Y\right]\|^{2}=4\|X\|^{2}\|Y\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\left[X,Y\right]\|^{2}=4\|X\|^{2}\|Y\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In order to characterize the equality condition of the DDVV-type inequality for quaternionic matrices, we introduce the following map.
Let</p>
<table id="S3.Ex14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex14X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi:M(n,\mathbb{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℍ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi:M(n,\mathbb{H})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\longrightarrow M(2n,\mathbb{C})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\longrightarrow M(2n,\mathbb{C}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex14Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X=X_{1}+X_{2}\mathbf{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐣</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X=X_{1}+X_{2}\mathbf{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\longmapsto\begin{pmatrix}X_{1}&amp;X_{2}\\
-\overline{X_{2}}&amp;\overline{X_{1}}\\
\end{pmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟼</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mtd><mtd><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\longmapsto\begin{pmatrix}X_{1}&amp;X_{2}\\
-\overline{X_{2}}&amp;\overline{X_{1}}\\
\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2}\in M(n,\mathbb{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2}\in M(n,\mathbb{C})</annotation></semantics></math>.
It is easy to see</p>
<table id="S3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Psi(X)\|^{2}=2\|X\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Psi(X)\|^{2}=2\|X\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y\in M(n,\mathbb{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℍ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y\in M(n,\mathbb{H})</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="S3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}:=[X_{1},Y_{1}]-X_{2}\overline{Y_{2}}+Y_{2}\overline{X_{2}},\quad A_{2}:=X_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{2}\overline{X_{1}}+X_{2}\overline{Y_{1}}-Y_{1}X_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}:=[X_{1},Y_{1}]-X_{2}\overline{Y_{2}}+Y_{2}\overline{X_{2}},\quad A_{2}:=X_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{2}\overline{X_{1}}+X_{2}\overline{Y_{1}}-Y_{1}X_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Then direct calculations show</p>
<table id="S3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[X,Y]=A_{1}+A_{2}\mathbf{j},\quad\left[\Psi(X),\Psi(Y)\right]=\begin{pmatrix}A_{1}&amp;A_{2}\\
-\overline{A_{2}}&amp;\overline{A_{1}}\\
\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐣</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mtd><mtd><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X,Y]=A_{1}+A_{2}\mathbf{j},\quad\left[\Psi(X),\Psi(Y)\right]=\begin{pmatrix}A_{1}&amp;A_{2}\\
-\overline{A_{2}}&amp;\overline{A_{1}}\\
\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Remember <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{j}\mathbf{i}=-\mathbf{i}\mathbf{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐣𝐢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐢𝐣</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{j}\mathbf{i}=-\mathbf{i}\mathbf{j}</annotation></semantics></math> when moving the <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to the right.
Therefore <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the commutator:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\Psi(X),\Psi(Y)\right]=\Psi(\left[X,Y\right])." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\Psi(X),\Psi(Y)\right]=\Psi(\left[X,Y\right]).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.7</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Ge-Li-Zhou <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>)<span id="S3.Thmthm7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1},\cdots,B_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1},\cdots,B_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be arbitrary <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times n</annotation></semantics></math> quaternionic matrices.</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
