<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Hence the optimal constants for the quaternionic matrices case
and the quaternionic skew-Hermitian matrices case are both
<math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{8}{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{8}{3}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math>. The equality condition could be also written in quaternion domain as in Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 3.4 (BW-type inequality for quaternionic matrices []). ‣ 3.2. DDVV-type inequality for quaternionic matrices ‣ 3. New progress on DDVV-type inequalities ‣ A survey on the DDVV-type inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>. A maximal triple <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B_{1},B_{2},B_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B_{1},B_{2},B_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> determines the <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P,R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P,R)</annotation></semantics></math>-action, and all others must be zero. The surviving matrices should be in the form</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

