<div id="S3.Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.9</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Ge-Li-Zhou <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>)<span id="S3.Thmthm9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{0},P_{1},\cdots,P_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{0},P_{1},\cdots,P_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> be a Clifford system on <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{2l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{2l}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0},\cdots,P_{m}\in O(2l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0},\cdots,P_{m}\in O(2l)</annotation></semantics></math> are real symmetric orthogonal matrices satisfying <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}P_{j}+P_{j}P_{i}=2\delta_{ij}I_{2l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}P_{j}+P_{j}P_{i}=2\delta_{ij}I_{2l}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1},\cdots,B_{M}\in span\{P_{0},P_{1},\cdots,P_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1},\cdots,B_{M}\in span\{P_{0},P_{1},\cdots,P_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{M}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\leq\frac{2}{l}\left(1-\frac{1}{N}\right)\left(\sum^{M}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2},\quad N=\min\{m+1,M\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{M}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\leq\frac{2}{l}\left(1-\frac{1}{N}\right)\left(\sum^{M}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2},\quad N=\min\{m+1,M\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The condition for equality has two cases.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1)</annotation></semantics></math>: When <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+1\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+1\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>, the equality holds if and only if
<math id="S3.Thmthm9.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0},\cdots,p_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0},\cdots,p_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are orthogonal vectors with the same norm,
where <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}:=\left(\langle P_{i},B_{1}\rangle,\cdots,\langle P_{i},B_{M}\rangle\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}:=\left(\langle P_{i},B_{1}\rangle,\cdots,\langle P_{i},B_{M}\rangle\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm9.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm9.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm9.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2)</annotation></semantics></math>: When <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+1\geq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+1\geq M</annotation></semantics></math>, the equality holds if and only if
<math id="S3.Thmthm9.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1},\cdots,B_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1},\cdots,B_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> are orthogonal matrices with the same Frobenius norm.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Analogously they were able to obtain the DDVV-type inequality for Clifford algebra.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.10</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Ge-Li-Zhou <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>)<span id="S3.Thmthm10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{E_{1},\cdots,E_{m-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{E_{1},\cdots,E_{m-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Clifford algebra on <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1},\cdots,E_{m-1}\in O(l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1},\cdots,E_{m-1}\in O(l)</annotation></semantics></math> are real skew-symmetric orthogonal matrices satisfying <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i}E_{j}+E_{j}E_{i}=-2\delta_{ij}I_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i}E_{j}+E_{j}E_{i}=-2\delta_{ij}I_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1},\cdots,B_{M}\in span\{E_{1},\cdots,E_{m-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1},\cdots,B_{M}\in span\{E_{1},\cdots,E_{m-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{M}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\leq\frac{4}{l}\left(1-\frac{1}{N}\right)\left(\sum^{M}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2},\quad N=\min\{m-1,M\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{M}_{r,s=1}\|\left[B_{r},B_{s}\right]\|^{2}\leq\frac{4}{l}\left(1-\frac{1}{N}\right)\left(\sum^{M}_{r=1}\|B_{r}\|^{2}\right)^{2},\quad N=\min\{m-1,M\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The condition for equality has two cases.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm10.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm10.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm10.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1)</annotation></semantics></math>: When <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-1\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-1\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>, the equality holds if and only if
<math id="S3.Thmthm10.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1},\cdots,e_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1},\cdots,e_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> are orthogonal with the same norm,
where <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}:=\left(\langle E_{i},B_{1}\rangle,\cdots,\langle E_{i},B_{M}\rangle\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}:=\left(\langle E_{i},B_{1}\rangle,\cdots,\langle E_{i},B_{M}\rangle\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm10.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm10.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm10.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2)</annotation></semantics></math>: When <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-1\geq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-1\geq M</annotation></semantics></math>, the equality holds if and only if
<math id="S3.Thmthm10.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1},\cdots,B_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1},\cdots,B_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> are orthogonal with the same norm.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4. </span>Lu inequality</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To prove DDVV conjecture, Lu <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite> discovered the stronger inequality below. Meanwhile, this inequality can also provide a new geometric pinching result (see Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmthm5" title="Theorem 2.5 (Lu[]). ‣ 2.1. DDVV inequality in submanifold geometry ‣ 2. The origin and applications in geometry ‣ A survey on the DDVV-type inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.11</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lu inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite>)<span id="S3.Thmthm11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times n</annotation></semantics></math> diagonal matrix of norm <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2},\cdots,A_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2},\cdots,A_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be symmetric matrices such that</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle A_{\alpha},A_{\beta}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle A_{\alpha},A_{\beta}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if </span><math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\neq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\neq\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
