<div id="S3.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For two real numbers </span><math id="S3.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1/\sqrt{n(n-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1/\sqrt{n(n-1)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, we have</span></p>
